---
import ActivityGuideLayout from '../layouts/ActivityGuideLayout.astro';
import ActivityOperators from '../components/ActivityOperators.astro';
const sections = [{ id: 'surfing', label: 'Surfing' }, { id: 'diving', label: 'Diving' }, { id: 'planning', label: 'Plan an ocean day' }, { id: 'operators', label: 'Local contacts' }];
---
<ActivityGuideLayout page="diving-and-surfing" title="Diving & Surfing in Pohnpei | P-Pass, Manta Road & Local Contacts" description="Explore Pohnpei’s reef breaks and dive sites, understand the conditions to discuss, and find published surf and dive contacts." sections={sections}>
  <section slot="hero" class="relative overflow-hidden bg-basalt"><div class="relative w-full aspect-[16/9] md:aspect-[21/9] min-h-[480px] md:min-h-[560px]">
    <img
          class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full object-cover opacity-60"
          src="https://res.cloudinary.com/doruy2kdr/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto,c_fill,g_auto,w_2000,h_900/hero-right-manta-road-pass.jpg"
          alt="Manta ray swimming through blue water"
          width="2000"
          height="900"
          fetchpriority="high"
        />
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-basalt/80 via-basalt/30 to-transparent"></div><div class="absolute inset-0 flex flex-col justify-end p-6 md:p-16 lg:p-24 max-w-4xl"><p class="text-xs tracking-[.2em] uppercase text-sand/90 mb-4">Pohnpei / Beyond the shore</p><h1 class="font-headline text-sand text-5xl md:text-6xl lg:text-7xl leading-[1.02] tracking-tight mb-5">Diving &amp; <em>surfing.</em></h1><p class="font-headline text-sand/90 text-xl md:text-2xl mb-7 max-w-lg">Reef breaks above. A different landscape below.</p><div><a href="#surfing" class="tg-button bg-sand text-basalt hover:bg-sand-bright">Explore the ocean guide ↓</a></div></div>
  </div></section>
  <section id="surfing" class="tg-section bg-sand"><div class="tg-wrap tg-split"><div><p class="tg-eyebrow">01 / Surfing</p><h2 class="tg-title">Palikir Pass.<br /><em>And beyond.</em></h2><p class="tg-copy">P-Pass is the familiar name for the right-hand break at Palikir Pass. Pohnpei’s offshore reef breaks call for experience and local knowledge. Arrange boat access and discuss conditions with a surf guide.</p><p class="tg-source">Background: <a class="tg-link" href="https://www.pohnpei-adventure.com/surfing/">Eco-Adventure surfing guide</a> · <a class="tg-link" href="https://visitpohnpei.travel/adventure/">Official adventure guide</a></p></div><div class="tg-copy"><h3 class="font-headline text-3xl text-basalt mb-4">Choose the conditions, then the break.</h3><p>Main Pass, Middle Pass and Lighthouse offer other possibilities. A smaller wave or a name such as “Easy Pass” does not remove the shallow-reef hazard. Ask a guide to match the day to your experience.</p><h3 class="font-headline text-3xl text-basalt mt-8 mb-4">When to discuss a trip</h3><p>The Eco-Adventure Guide places the main surf period around October–April, emphasizing January and February. Its exact season boundaries vary by section. Treat this as a broad planning window; confirm swell, wind, tide and boat access for your dates.</p><p class="tg-note mt-6">Tell your guide about your reef-break experience and equipment. Ask what would make them change the spot or cancel the outing.</p></div></div></section>
  <section id="diving" class="tg-section bg-sand-bright"><div class="tg-wrap"><div class="tg-split mb-9"><div><p class="tg-eyebrow">02 / Diving</p><h2 class="tg-title">Lagoon, walls<br /><em>and passages.</em></h2></div><div class="tg-copy"><p>Pohnpei’s dive sites span lagoon reefs, passes and outer walls. Currents and visibility vary with tide, rain and location. Share your certification and recent experience so a dive operator can propose suitable sites.</p><p class="tg-source">Background: <a class="tg-link" href="https://www.pohnpei-adventure.com/scuba/">Eco-Adventure SCUBA guide ↗</a></p></div></div><div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-8"><article class="border-t border-basalt/25 pt-6"><h3 class="font-headline text-3xl mb-4">Manta Road</h3><p class="tg-copy">A channel near Mwahnd Peidak known for manta encounters. The site guide describes strong currents; let a local dive professional decide whether and when it suits your group. Wildlife sightings are never assured.</p><p class="tg-source"><a class="tg-link" href="https://www.pohnpei-adventure.com/northside-diving/">North-side dive sites ↗</a></p></article><article class="border-t border-basalt/25 pt-6"><h3 class="font-headline text-3xl mb-4">Mwahnd Wall</h3><p class="tg-copy">The north-side guide describes a coral wall near the reef passage and classifies the dive as advanced. Ask about the proposed depth, current, required experience and any access permissions.</p><p class="tg-source"><a class="tg-link" href="https://www.pohnpei-adventure.com/northside-diving/">North-side dive sites ↗</a></p></article><article class="border-t border-basalt/25 pt-6"><h3 class="font-headline text-3xl mb-4">Ahnd &amp; Pakin</h3><p class="tg-copy">Both atolls have outer-reef diving described in the Eco-Adventure Guide. Open-water travel and local access arrangements make these separate planning conversations. Ask whether the trip is feasible before choosing a dive site.</p><a href="/outer-atolls" class="tg-page-link tg-link text-sm mt-4">Read the outer-island guide →</a><p class="tg-source"><a class="tg-link" href="https://www.pohnpei-adventure.com/atolls/">Ahnd &amp; Pakin background ↗</a></p></article></div></div></section>
  <section id="planning" class="tg-section bg-sand"><div class="tg-wrap tg-split"><div><p class="tg-eyebrow">03 / Before the boat</p><h2 class="tg-title">Make the details<br /><em>part of the plan.</em></h2><p class="tg-copy">Ask these questions before agreeing on an ocean outing. Keep room in the visit for changed conditions and discuss alternatives with your provider.</p><a href="/getting-here" class="tg-page-link tg-link mt-5">Check your journey &amp; airline information →</a></div><dl class="tg-rows tg-copy"><div><dt>Experience &amp; equipment</dt><dd>For diving, confirm required certification, supervision and available equipment in your size. For surfing, discuss boards and spares with your guide. Check your airline’s current equipment allowance.</dd></div><div><dt>Route &amp; return</dt><dd>Confirm the meeting point, boat arrangements, expected return and what happens if conditions change. Ask the operator about its communication and emergency procedures.</dd></div><div><dt>Permissions &amp; costs</dt><dd>Ask who secures landowner consent or protected-area permission and whether the quote includes these arrangements, equipment and boat transport.</dd></div><div><dt>Respect the reef</dt><dd>Leave space around wildlife and avoid touching or standing on coral. Follow the local briefing and ask about site restrictions before entering the water.</dd></div></dl></div></section>
  <section id="operators" class="tg-section bg-sand-bright"><div class="tg-wrap tg-split"><div><p class="tg-eyebrow">04 / Start a conversation</p><h2 class="tg-title">Find your<br /><em>ocean contact.</em></h2><p class="tg-copy">The tourism office lists these businesses for diving or ocean excursions. Ask what they currently operate and which sites they can arrange.</p><p class="tg-source">Services and contacts: <a class="tg-link" href="https://visitpohnpei.travel/tour-operators/">Official tourism directory ↗</a></p><a href="/tour-operators?service=ocean#directory" class="tg-button bg-basalt text-sand hover:bg-lagoon mt-6">Compare ocean contacts →</a><div class="tg-note mt-8"><h3 class="font-headline text-2xl mb-3">For surfing</h3><p class="tg-copy">The Eco-Adventure surfing guide names Pohnpei Surf Club as a surf-guide contact. Use its tourism-listed contact details to ask about current surf trips.</p><ActivityOperators place="p-pass" /></div></div><ActivityOperators service="ocean" /></div></section>
</ActivityGuideLayout>
